\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Happy the heart where graces reign,
\par Where love inspires the breast;
\par Love is the brightest of the train,
\par And perfects all the rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Knowledge, alas, 'tis all in vain,
\par And all in vain our fear;
\par Our stubborn sins will fight and reign,
\par If love be absent there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. 'Tis love that makes our cheerful feet,
\par In swift obedience move:
\par The devils know, and tremble too;
\par But Satan cannot love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. This is the grace that lives and sings,
\par When faith and hope shall cease;
\par 'Tis this shall strike our joyful strings,
\par In the sweet realm of bliss.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Before we quite forsake our clay,
\par Or leave this dark abode,
\par The wings of love bear us away
\par To see our gracious God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

